[line]
[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
Every feature is individually toggleable via [url=https://github.com/sonofskywalker3/GenericModConfigMenu/releases]Generic Mod Config Menu[/url] or config.json:
[list]
[*]Controller Layout (Switch / Xbox / PlayStation)
[*]Control Style (Switch-style or Xbox-style confirm/cancel)
[*]Console Chests (sorting, transfer, color picker, sidebar)
[*]Console Shops (A purchases, quantity control, sell tab, full-stack barter trades)
[*]Console Animal Menu (sell / move animals with the controller)
[*]Console Toolbar (12-slot rows, bumper/trigger switching)
[*]Console Inventory (A/Y item management, bait/tackle)
[*]Console Shipping (A/Y ship controls)
[*]Console Menus (all game menu tab navigation)
[*]Console Furniture Placement (single ghost rectangle, craftables + seeds too)
[*]Console Museum Donation + Geode menus
[*]Move While Charging (charge Hoe/Watering Can while walking)
[*]Console Slingshot Aim
[*]Console Drop Blocker
[*]Console Dialogue Cursor
[*]Pickup To Active Row
[*]Hold To Craft
[*]Right Stick Cursor
[*]Carpenter Menu Fix
[*]Furniture Debounce
[*]Hold Start for Quest Log
[*]Bumper Mode
[*]And more
[/list]
(Zoom level and the tool-hit-location checkboxes live on the in-game Options page and now persist across restarts.)

[line]
[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Stardew Valley 1.6.15+ (Android)
[*][url=https://github.com/NRTnarathip/SMAPI-Android-1.6]SMAPI 4.0+ for Android[/url] by NRTnarathip
[*][url=https://github.com/sonofskywalker3/GenericModConfigMenu/releases]Generic Mod Config Menu[/url] (optional, recommended — our fork adds controller navigation)
[/list]

[line]
[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
New to modding on Android? The whole thing takes about five minutes. Mods do [b]not[/b] go through the "Install SMAPI From Zip" button; that button only accepts SMAPI's own zip, and it will refuse a mod zip with a "Please select file SMAPI-4.x.x.xxxx.zip" error.

[b]1. Install SMAPI (one time only)[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install the SMAPI Launcher app from [url=https://github.com/NRTnarathip/SMAPILoader/releases]github.com/NRTnarathip/SMAPILoader/releases[/url].
[*]Download SMAPI.4.x.x-(xxxx).zip from [url=https://github.com/NRTnarathip/SMAPI-Android-1.6/releases]github.com/NRTnarathip/SMAPI-Android-1.6/releases[/url] into your Download folder. Don't unzip it.
[*]Open SMAPI Launcher, tap [b]Install SMAPI From Zip[/b], and pick that SMAPI zip.
[*]Wait for the "Successfully Install SMAPI" message.
[/list]

[b]2. Install the mod[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download AndroidConsolizer.X.Y.Z.zip from the Files tab. Don't unzip it.
[*]In SMAPI Launcher, tap [b]Mod Manager[/b], then [b]Install Mod[/b], and pick the Android Consolizer zip.
[*]It will confirm the install and Android Consolizer will appear in the Found Mods list. Do the same for any other mod zip, such as Generic Mod Config Menu.
[/list]

[b]3. Launch the game[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Back on the launcher's main screen, tap [b]Start Game[/b]. Always start from SMAPI Launcher, never the normal Stardew icon; the regular icon runs the plain game with no mods.
[*]You'll know it worked when the toolbar shows 12 slots with a controller connected.
[/list]

If something goes wrong, use the launcher's [b]Share Log[/b] button and post the link on the Nexus bugs tab along with which step failed.

